"A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"Grignard product is that product which forms because of nucleophilic addition reaction.\n<br><br>Aldehydes on reaction with Grignard reagent gives Grignard product.\n<br><br><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/h3NZMVM0QClPGBbH9/VBfLaJNaYAmLk9dItpUoXPOGFdOyk/Zi34ARda5h3eNpDx9nD3xw/image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%;  height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2019 (Online) 12th January Evening Slot Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 231 English Explanation 1\">\n<br><br>In Grignard reagent R<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup> is a very strong base, so it will react with acidic H<sup>+</sup> of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>COOH group first. As Grignard reagent is one equivalent, so no reagent will remain to react with aldehyde group.\n<br><br><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/0SEIU3xB12FaJBRzp/AdsmtmCig19KceVEnxuQolFHpTepi/z41ngSTzfFze0voaZKwZB0/image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%;  height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2019 (Online) 12th January Evening Slot Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 231 English Explanation 2\">\n<br><br>Here also in alcohol functional group (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>CH<sub>2</sub>OH)  H<sup>+</sup> is acidic so here acid base reaction will occur.\n<br><br>In option (A) only one functional group (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> CHO) present so it will give Grignard product by nucleofilic addition reaction.\n<br><br>In option (C) functional group ether (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> CH<sub>3</sub>) does not react with RMgX so aldehyde functional group will react with RMgX and give Grignard product. \n<br><br><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/xSnbPjA1QkamJ9llK/WsCVRxDrwxzwEQbAXxhxvnlEdZ6TO/3z94WiNq3M5uo9UrwrN34F/image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%;  height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2019 (Online) 12th January Evening Slot Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 231 English Explanation 3\">"},"hi":{"content":"वह एल्डिहाइड जो एक समान Grognard प्रतिक्रियाकारकों के साथ Grognard उत्पाद नहीं बनाएगा - \n<br><br><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/6MlwjiiiTaVxM5QQm/J8vg4x2hP90ff3eDRTQSem3SoHDHh/L5FFkOzeGZAT8l5eRlcIze/image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%;  height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2019 (Online) 12th January Evening Slot Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 231 Hindi\">","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"B and D"},{"identifier":"B","content":"C and D"},{"identifier":"C","content":"B, C and D"},{"identifier":"D","content":"B and C"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":null,"comprehension":null,"direction":null}},"question_id":"3V67IKAULyqeDIlG1Z4VR","permalink":"the-aldehydes-which-will-not-form-grignard-product-with-one-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-0rkmu5wgjw4tdmdx","updated_time":1552639584,"timeAllotted":120000,"paperId":"jee-main-2019-online-12th-january-evening-slot","topic":"chemical-reactions-for-aldehydes-and-ketones","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["multi_statements"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2019-online-12th-january-evening-slot","active":true}],"ids":["WuxX0SVyhNlwREz1yOcAy","Ainno7Izmjbmyh82TDvpK","Xkt3Z5e1iJDUA6qApFldi","3V67IKAULyqeDIlG1Z4VR"],"title":"JEE Main 2019 (Online) 12th January Evening Slot | JEE Main Year Wise Previous Years Questions","canoni